      "message": "Before this CL, `deleteRuntimeArtifacts` treats the \"\\*\" in the `isa` field as a normal string and deletes the runtime artifacts in the folder named \"\\*\". After this CL, `deleteRuntimeArtifacts` treats the \"\\*\" in the `isa` field as invalid input and does nothing, so a file like `/data/user/0/com.android.foo/cache/oat_primary/*/base.art` is not interesting for this test anymore.\n\nThis behavior change is fine as explained in the comment above the test case: since the caller is never supposed to use a wildcard, as long as `deleteRuntimeArtifacts` doesn\u0027t treat \"\\*\" as a wildcard, either behavior is acceptable.",
